  "findings": [
    "claude: the recruiter was rejected four times (missing_work_unit, staff_without_safe_team twice, then review_reviewer_reused on unit-independent-review) and the turn ended preflight_failed with review_reviewer_reused on the receipt: the new rule fired live and is named on the durable receipt, but the recruiter's repair budget was already spent on coverage failures, so no repaired independent team was reached.",
    "hermes: the recruiter ranked only code-reviewer on the review unit (executable ranking of one), so no independent covering team existed and the verifier added nothing, as designed; the strict critic then vetoed the test-code unit with a wrong-neighbor-selection claim carrying a verified pointer (document-generator -> python-application-engineer), the first live receipt row for the AR-433 pointer contract.",
    "zcode: the recruiter again ranked only code-reviewer on the review unit; the reuse was accepted with no finding and the critic approved, consistent with the rule's no-alternative branch.",
    "openclaw: the recruiter failed on missing_work_unit and staff_without_safe_team across four attempts on a four-unit plan and the turn ended inference_invalid; unrelated to this rule.",
    "Follow-up: the rule can only bite when the recruiter ranks an independent reviewer; the recruiter contract does not yet ask it to, so a recruiter that ranks a single reviewer on a review unit leaves the reuse in place. Steering the recruiter to rank at least one reviewer not selected on the reviewed units is the next bounded lift."
